// Distributed 2D-grid schedule: 4 compute workers in a 2x2 grid via
// `partition=blocks2d`, async input streaming, sync output.
//
// This is the FIRST e2e cell exercising the halo-strip Push/Wait
// synthesis pass (TASK-0289 cycle 114a + TASK-0290 cycle 114b's
// placement fix). Currently [[skip]]ped in e2e-matrix.toml on
// TASK-0294: backend-common's `leading_axis_slice` (HONEST-PARTIAL
// ASSUMPTION from TASK-0117) ignores the inner axis of 2D partition
// tiles, so the host gather pastes each worker's 2D rectangle as a
// 1D y-band slice, overwriting adjacent workers' columns with
// default-zero values. Bit-identical against the existing
// 05-stencil/reference.bin would hold if the 2D slice-paste path
// landed (TASK-0294) — a SINGLE-PASS box blur is invariant under
// the partition SHAPE, so the same reference oracle applies
// regardless of whether the partition is 1D row-band
// (`distributed.sched.nuc`, partition=rows) or 2D grid (this file,
// partition=blocks2d).
//
// What this cell PROVES:
//   - partition=blocks2d lowers end-to-end on a tier-1 backend
//     (pthreads-async).
//   - The halo-strip Push/Wait synthesis pass (TASK-0289 AC#1) does
//     not break existing behaviour on a structurally-redundant
//     case — for a single-pass stencil with host-broadcast img_in,
//     the halo strips carry data the host broadcast already
//     provides (each worker's img_in tile is extended by halo via
//     `extend_xfer_tiles_for_halo` already in TASK-0263).
//   - TASK-0290 cycle 114b placement fix: the synthesised pairs
//     land in the root Sequence AFTER the host's `load_image`
//     Operation, so the per-worker EventList orders the halo-strip
//     Wait AFTER the host has produced the data.
//
// What this cell does NOT prove (deferred to TASK-0294):
//   - Multi-pass / iterative-stencil halo exchange where each
//     worker owns its tile across timesteps and the cross-worker
//     halo strips carry semantically-unique data.
//   - Halo-strip placement INSIDE a time-step Repeat body (the
//     current placement is once, at the root Sequence level).
//
// Image dimensions + 2x2-grid divisibility (load-bearing math):
//   - 05-stencil/prog.algo.nuc: H = W = 16; the compute loops walk
//     y in 1..H-1 = 1..15 (length 14) and x in 1..W-1 = 1..15
//     (length 14).
//   - decompose_grid(4) returns (rows=2, cols=2); 14 / 2 = 7 rows
//     and 7 cols per worker. 14 % 2 == 0 ⇒ exact-divisible on both
//     axes (no spillover policy invoked).
//   - Per-worker assignment (row-major over BTreeSet numeric
//     WorkerId order — matches partition_blocks2d.rs's `for (i,
//     wid) in body_workers.iter().enumerate() { row = i / cols;
//     col = i % cols }`):
//       w0 (0,0): y=1..8,  x=1..8     w1 (0,1): y=1..8,  x=8..15
//       w2 (1,0): y=8..15, x=1..8     w3 (1,1): y=8..15, x=8..15
//   - halo_y = halo_x = 1 (inferred from blur3's 3x3 access).
//
// Backends:
//   - pthreads-async: [[required]] in e2e-matrix.toml. The
//     capability surface (async + buffer + notify=event) matches
//     the `transfer img_in` directive below.
//   - pthreads-sync + mp-tcp-bufsync: SKIP on capability mismatch
//     (no async/buffer/event), same as today's distributed
//     schedule sibling.
//   - mp-tcp-event: SKIP on TASK-0175 lineage (w↔w mesh required
//     for the halo strips' worker-to-worker transfers, which
//     mp-tcp-event's host-star topology cannot lower). NOTE this
//     differs from `distributed.sched.nuc` where mp-tcp-event was
//     ultimately promoted in cycle 102 (TASK-0268) because the
//     row-band partition's halo strips happen to land in the
//     existing host-broadcast extension and need no genuine w↔w
//     transfer; the 2x2-grid partition does need real worker-to-
//     worker E/W strips between (row, 0) and (row, 1) which the
//     mp-tcp-event star cannot mediate.

schedule for "../prog.algo.nuc" {
    workers = { host, w0, w1, w2, w3 };

    place load_image on host;
    place save_image on host;
    place blur3      on { w0, w1, w2, w3 };

    // 2x2-grid partition over the outer y-loop. The directive pairs
    // the outer y-loop with the inner x-loop via the partition_pairs
    // sidecar (TASK-0264 cycle 113); the halo-strip synthesis pass
    // (TASK-0289 cycle 114a) reads partition_pairs +
    // grid_shape_for_outer_iv + halo_widths to emit one Push/Wait
    // pair per (neighbour, data, axis) for the 4 cardinal neighbours
    // (N/S/W/E; corners are out-of-scope per TASK-0264's task
    // brief).
    loop y : partition=blocks2d;

    // host -> workers: async streaming, two row-bands in flight.
    // Same shape as distributed.sched.nuc's `img_in` directive —
    // forces this cell onto the pthreads-async backend exclusively
    // (the two sync backends reject at capability check).
    transfer img_in  : async, buffer=2, notify=event;

    // workers -> host: simple blocking write-back. Host waits for
    // all workers to finish before save_image runs.
    transfer img_out : sync;
}
